{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And he released him.</b> The angel. And so we find this expression used of the angel, as it is said (I Chronicles 21:15): ״ויאמר למלאך המשחית רב עתה הרף ידך״ — 'And he said to the destroying angel: It is enough; now release your hand'; and this was after she had cut the foreskin of her son." "<b>And it is possible</b> to explain that since Scripture used the expression 'and he released him' and did not say 'and he departed from him,' the angel hinted to her that the commandment was not yet complete. And immediately Tziporah understood this, completed the commandment, and performed for him פריעה (the uncovering). From this she said ״חתן דמים למולות״ — 'a bridegroom of blood for circumcisions,' meaning two circumcision-acts: מילה and פריעה. And the reason it mentions חתן דמים twice is to indicate that liability of death was incurred for the מילה and liability was incurred for the פריעה, for both are indispensable."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:11.501562115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}